ResCurrentState [SimTalk] - fluid objects
Returns the current state of the fluid object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
During a simulation run a material flow resource can take on one of these states: Working, Setting-up,
Waiting, Blocked, Failed, Stopped, Paused, Powering Up/down, or Unplanned.
Note
If two states occur at the same time, for example Paused and Failed, the read-only attribute returns the
state that also has precedence for statistics collection. Paused for example for Paused and Failed.
Type
Read-only attribute
Syntax
<Path>.ResCurrentState → string
Watchable
The read-only attribute is watchable.
Use it in waituntil-instructions or to make the object TimeSequence record it in watch mode.
Return Value
The return value has the data type string.
Example
print MyMixer.ResCurrentState
See also
Resource Statistics [material flow objects]
Working [state, material flow objects], Setting-Up [state, material flow objects], Waiting [state,
material flow objects], Blocked [state, material flow objects], Failed [state - material flow objects],
Stopped [state, material flow objects], Paused [state, material flow objects], Powering up/down
[state, material flow objects], Unplanned [state, material flow objects]
ResCurrentState [SimTalk] - fluid objects
